This is 100% legal and widely done.

🧩 How modders usually handle “inspired by another game” mods
They follow three rules:

1. No direct asset ports
Everything must be rebuilt using Fallout assets or custom-made meshes.

2. Layout can be similar
Copyright does not protect “room layout” or “general architecture.”

3. Replace iconic copyrighted elements
Exactly what you suggested:

Replace Mistle → Fast travel activator

Replace Code Vein props → Nuka‑Cola machines, BOS crates, terminals

Replace Code Vein NPCs → Fallout merchants or settlers

This transforms it from “copyright infringement” into “Fallout‑themed homage.”

